invariant: INV-74
file: src/handshake_post.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh key_update_seal
reason: hspost_seal_key_update returns CH_ECAP with whatever length
  rec_seal wrote when it refused the record. record.h states no length
  for a refused record, and handshake_post.h states 0. The real rec_seal
  writes none, so no test of the record layer sees it; the proof's
  rec_seal stub writes any length and requires the 0.

--- old
        *out_len = 0; // record.h states no length for a record it refused
        return CH_ECAP;
--- new
        return CH_ECAP;
